WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:07.128
In the Later Zhou of the Five Dynasties, General Guo Wei, in his forties, was a seasoned veteran.

00:00:07.478 --> 00:00:16.046
One day, the soldiers gathered together, loudly calling for Guo Wei to become emperor.

00:00:16.396 --> 00:00:21.964
The soldiers brought a yellow banner and solemnly draped it over Guo Wei's shoulders.

00:00:22.314 --> 00:00:27.402
Guo Wei looked at everyone in surprise, speechless for a moment.

00:00:27.752 --> 00:00:34.184
This was the famous 'Yellow Banner Draping' — and so Guo Wei ascended the throne.

00:00:34.534 --> 00:00:37.558
From then on, Guo Wei founded the Later Zhou dynasty.

00:00:37.908 --> 00:00:44.868
A few years later, Zhao Kuangyin met the same fate, as soldiers draped a yellow robe over him.

00:00:45.218 --> 00:00:51.818
The two yellow-draping stories are often compared, becoming a beloved tale of history.

00:00:52.168 --> 00:00:55.816
Whenever people tell these two stories, they always relish them.

